 "headline": [
  "Every public server but Cloudflare docs ships server instructions over 512 chars (632–6,731), which ChatGPT cuts and claude.ai chat and ChatGPT Work do not deliver at all.",
  "DeepWiki keeps its guidance in the instructions (3,097 chars against 212 in all three tool descriptions), so on claude.ai chat and ChatGPT Work the model gets the tool names and little else.",
  "Descriptions are short everywhere (only Hugging Face hf_fs, 2,875, passes Claude Code 2,048), and input schemas stay under Codex 5,000 except GitHub projects_write (7,035) in the all-toolsets build.",
  "GitHub re-sends 123,729 chars of tool definitions per turn with its default toolsets and 256,560 with all 90 tools."
 ],
